// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2852774960" "These recent Rikti thefts have me worried. There's only one reason I can think of for the Rikti to go around stealing human blood and organs. They must be trying to improve their mutagen so that it transforms people more quickly! From what is known about the current Rikti mutagen, they will need a large supply of the chemical Barizium. The only place I could find that had a lot of Barizium in stock was Nicholson Chemicals over in Independence Port. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>You should get over there to protect their warehouse so the Rikti can't make off with the Barizium.</A>"
// AcceptString :
"P3022582399" "Protect Nicholson Chemicals"
// SendOffString :
"P2180439920" "Keep those chemicals out of the Rikti's hands, {HeroName}."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3295410402" "Defeat all villains in warehouse"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P4009036062" "You need to make Paragon City as safe as possible, {HeroName}. You know what to do."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P2255701542" "The upper levels were empty, abandoned. You soon found a staircase leading down to a sub-basement, and quickly realized this was no ordinary warehouse, but a front for a Council base!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3423024075" "The Council base has been cleaned out."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2724698564" "It wasn't a chemical company, but a Council front? Well, we lucked out on that one. Still, I'm sure the Rikti are up to something. Why else would they go around stealing human organs and blood? We've got to get back on their trail."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P171341662" "It looks like that warehouse I sent you to was a dead end. Even worse, the Rikti struck while you were over there! They kidnapped the renowned transplant specialist Dr. Samuel Snider, right out of his operating room! We have a hot trail to follow, {HeroName}. <A HREF={ACCEPT}>I need you to rescue Dr. Snider.</A>"
// AcceptString :
"P4294819203" "Rescue Dr. Snider"
// SendOffString :
"P1444492409" "Dr. Snider was wearing his pager, so we should be able to track that to where he is being held. Hurry, {HeroName}, before it's too late!"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1247186967" "Find Dr. Snider"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3968212743" "You need to get back Dr. Snider. Follow the signal to his pager!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P2422247326" "The triangulator has too much interference to precisely locate the pager in here, but it is close."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - VILLAIN_GROUP 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - PATROLLER1_SEARCHING_DIALOG 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - PATROLLER2_SEARCHING_DIALOG 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - PATROLLER_ATTACK_DIALOG1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

